<title>THAILAND: Thai Sept CPI up 4.6 pct yr/yr, 0.1 pct mth/mth.</title>
<headline>Thai Sept CPI up 4.6 pct yr/yr, 0.1 pct mth/mth.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Thai consumer price index (CPI) rose 4.6 percent year-on-year in September and 0.1 percent month-on-month, the Commerce Ministry said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The ministry said the 1990-based index rose 4.6 percent year-on-year in September to 135.0, up from the 129.1 level in September 1995.</p>
<p>The 0.1 percent month-on-month increase compared to a 1.0 percent rise in August over July, the ministry said.</p>
<p>The index rose 5.5 percent year-on-year in August.  </p>
<p>The Thai Commerce Ministry issued the following economic indicators:</p>
<p>     THAI CONSUMER PRICES	 Sept 96	Aug 96	Sept 95</p>
<p>     Month/month			0.1	   +1.0	  +1.0</p>
<p>     Year/year			  4.6	   +5.5	  +6.2</p>
<p>     CPI Index (base 1990)	135.0	  134.8	 129.1</p>
<p>     Food/beverage Index	  146.1	  145.9	 136.4</p>
<p>     Month/month		     +0.1	   +2.3	  +2.0</p>
<p>     Year/year			 +7.1	   +9.1	  +8.1</p>
<p>     Non food/beverage Index    127.6	  127.4	 124.3</p>
<p>     Month/month		     +0.2	   +0.0	  +0.3</p>
<p>     Year/year			 +2.7	   +2.8	  +4.9</p>
</text>
